1
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:25,010
Champagne flutes on the limestone ledge

2
00:00:25,130 --> 00:00:27,230
Three dozen stories above the avenue hedge

3
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:30,110
You’re leaning back in your linen shirt

4
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:34,710
Laughing too loud so the truth won't hurt

5
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:38,990
The sun drops low like a minted coin

6
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:43,340
Where the rusted girders and brick adjoin

7
00:00:43,390 --> 00:00:46,130
Everyone’s acting like August stayed

8
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:50,190
While the terrace shadows begin to trade

9
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:54,170
There’s a sudden bite in the evening air

10
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:58,030
And you trace the rim of your crystal ware

11
00:00:58,080 --> 00:01:02,470
You look at the skyline, not at me

12
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:06,620
Like a ship already out to sea

13
00:02:10,760 --> 00:03:18,430
It’s copper on the terrace, gold turning to rust

14
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:22,390
All of our promises ground into velvet dust

15
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:26,390
Dance me to the edge of the balcony rail

16
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:31,320
Before the warm trade winds begin to fail

17
00:03:31,370 --> 00:03:34,170
You’re holding my waist like a souvenir

18
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:38,250
In the brightest hour of a dying year

19
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:39,230
Yeah, it’s copper on the terrace tonight

20
00:03:39,280 --> 00:01:43,630
Your best friend’s spinning an old French record

21
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:47,410
Our history’s suddenly strangely checkered

22
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:51,300
You hand me your jacket, the lining’s torn

23
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:55,030
Swearing this fever is newly born

24
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:58,900
But I know the cadence of an exit line

25
00:01:58,980 --> 00:02:02,710
Dressed up in vintage cabernet wine

26
00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:06,230
You kiss my collarbone, quick and polite

27
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:10,440
Beneath the amber Edison string-bulb light

28
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:14,480
There’s a sudden bite in the evening air

29
00:02:14,580 --> 00:02:18,310
And you trace the rim of your crystal ware

30
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:22,030
You look at the skyline, not at me

31
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:26,060
Like a ship already out to sea

32
00:02:26,180 --> 00:02:30,000
It’s copper on the terrace, gold turning to rust

33
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:33,980
All of our promises ground into velvet dust

34
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:37,980
Dance me to the edge of the balcony rail

35
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:41,980
Before the warm trade winds begin to fail

36
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:45,980
You’re holding my waist like a souvenir

37
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:49,980
In the brightest hour of a dying year

38
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:55,680
Yeah, it’s copper on the terrace tonight

39
00:02:58,180 --> 00:03:00,230
Remember July on the fire escape?

40
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:02,130
When every tomorrow had a reckless shape!

41
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:03,930
Now you’re folding your secrets into your cuff

42
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:05,730
As if wanting you once wasn't quite enough!

43
00:03:05,780 --> 00:03:08,130
Don't tell me the season is just a phase

44
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:13,360
When I see the frost in your sideways gaze!

45
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:17,580
It’s copper on the terrace, gold turning to rust!

46
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:21,580
All of our promises ground into velvet dust!

47
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:25,410
Dance me to the edge of the balcony rail

48
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:29,290
Before the warm trade winds begin to fail!

49
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:33,280
You’re holding my waist like a souvenir

50
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:38,980
In the brightest hour of a dying year

51
00:03:39,910 --> 00:03:46,120
Yeah, it’s copper on the terrace tonight!

52
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:50,750
Copper and rust on the avenue

53
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:55,050
The air turns sharp between me and you

54
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:58,130
Just a souvenir

55
00:03:58,180 --> 00:04:03,000
in the fading glow
